---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
const repo = 'https://github.com/zbcoding/ImpastoPaint';
const appPrivacyPolicy = `${repo}/blob/main/docs/privacy-policy.md`;
const license = `${repo}/blob/main/license-mit.txt`;
const thirdPartyNotices = `${repo}/blob/main/THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md`;
---
<Layout
  lang="en"
  title="Privacy Policy — Impasto"
  description="Privacy policy for the impastopaint.com website: what the cookieless analytics record, which services handle requests, and where the Impasto application's own policy lives."
  localeAlternates={false}
>
  <header class="page-header">
    <div class="wrap row">
      <a href={`${base}/`} class="brand">
        <img src={`${base}/assets/impasto-logo.svg`} width="28" height="28" alt="" />
        <span>Impasto</span>
      </a>
      <nav>
        <a href={`${base}/docs/`}>Docs</a>
        <a href={`${repo}/releases`}>Download</a>
        <a href={repo}>GitHub</a>
      </nav>
    </div>
  </header>

  <main class="wrap policy">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>

    <section>
      <h2>Scope</h2>
      <p>
        This policy covers the website at <strong>impastopaint.com</strong>, including
        <strong>www.impastopaint.com</strong> and its documentation pages. The Impasto
        application you download and run has its own policy, linked under
        <a href="#application">The Impasto application</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Definitions</h2>
      <p><strong>Personal data:</strong> any information relating to an identified or identifiable natural person.</p>
      <p><strong>Processing:</strong> any operation performed on personal data, such as collection, recording, storage, use, or disclosure.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <p>
        The website has no accounts, sign-ups, forms, comments, or advertising. It does not ask
        for your name or email address. The only data collected is the page-visit information
        recorded by the analytics services below, and the request logs kept by the hosting
        provider.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Analytics</h2>
      <p>
        We measure visits with two cookieless analytics services. Neither uses cookies or local
        storage, and both apply to visitors in all regions, including the EU, EEA, and UK.
      </p>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Service</th><th>What it records</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>GoatCounter</td>
            <td>The page visited, page title, referring page, screen size, and query string. Visits from local or embedded pages are not counted.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Cloudflare Web Analytics, provided by Cloudflare, Inc.</td>
            <td>Page load speed and performance, the page visited, the referring page, and your browser and device type. Cloudflare states that it does not fingerprint visitors.</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p>Both services receive your IP address as part of the request; Impasto does not store it.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Third-party data processors</h2>
      <p>These services handle requests to the website on our behalf:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>GitHub Pages</strong>, provided by GitHub, Inc. — hosts the website. GitHub processes your IP address and request details when it serves a page.</li>
        <li><strong>GoatCounter</strong> — page-view analytics, as described above.</li>
        <li><strong>Cloudflare Web Analytics</strong> — performance and page-view analytics, as described above.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Links to GitHub, such as downloads, releases, and the issue tracker, take you to GitHub's
        own site, where GitHub's privacy policy applies.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Purpose and legal basis</h2>
      <p>
        Analytics tell us which pages people read and how fast they load, so we can improve the
        documentation and the site. Processing is based on our legitimate interest in running and
        improving the website.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Cookies</h2>
      <p>
        The website sets no cookies and uses no local storage. Neither analytics service sets
        cookies either.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Your choices</h2>
      <p>
        You can stop the analytics from running by blocking scripts from
        <code>static.cloudflareinsights.com</code> and requests to <code>goatcounter.com</code>,
        for example with a content blocker. The site works the same without them. Your IP address
        still reaches the hosting provider, because a page cannot be delivered without it.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        You may have the right to access, correct, or delete your data, and to limit its
        processing. To exercise these rights, open an issue on the
        <a href={`${repo}/issues`}>GitHub issue tracker</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="application">
      <h2>The Impasto application</h2>
      <p>
        The Impasto application does not send your images, settings, or usage data anywhere. It
        makes a few network requests, such as checking for updates and refreshing the add-in
        gallery, which are listed in the
        <a href={appPrivacyPolicy}>application privacy policy</a> in the repository.
      </p>
      <p>
        Impasto is free and open source. Its terms of use are the
        <a href={license}>MIT License</a>, with third-party attributions in
        <a href={thirdPartyNotices}>THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Policy changes</h2>
      <p>We may update this policy from time to time. Changes are recorded in the repository's history.</p>
    </section>

    <p class="updated">Last updated: November 5, 2026</p>
  </main>
</Layout>

<style>
  .wrap { max-width: 1040px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 1.5rem; }
  .row { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 1rem; }

  .page-header { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); padding: 1rem 0; }
  .brand { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.5rem; font-weight: 700; font-size: 1.15rem; color: var(--fg); text-decoration: none; }
  .page-header nav { display: flex; gap: 1.25rem; }
  .page-header nav a { color: var(--fg-muted); text-decoration: none; font-size: 0.95rem; }
  .page-header nav a:hover { color: var(--fg); }

  .policy { max-width: 780px; padding-top: 2rem; padding-bottom: 4rem; }
  .policy h1 { font-size: clamp(1.7rem, 3.2vw, 2.3rem); margin: 0 0 1.5rem; }
  .policy h2 { font-size: 1.3rem; margin: 2.2rem 0 0.75rem; padding-top: 0.5rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .policy p, .policy li { color: #d5d9e4; }
  .policy li { margin: 0.3rem 0; }
  .policy table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin: 1.25rem 0; font-size: 0.93rem; display: block; overflow-x: auto; }
  .policy th, .policy td { border: 1px solid var(--border); padding: 0.45rem 0.7rem; text-align: left; vertical-align: top; }
  .policy th { background: var(--bg-raised); }
  .updated { margin-top: 3rem; font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--fg-muted) !important; }
</style>
